{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Make me remember.</b> And if you say that you did not sin against Me while you were in your land, and that I exiled you for nothing — make me remember:" "<b>Let us be judged together.</b> Let us stand for judgment:" "<b>Recount.</b> Your own words, so that you may be justified:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {0 "The lemma translates the divine suffix as 'Me' since the speaker throughout is YHWH addressing Israel."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:50.059803759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}